      "message": "Hi @vishnunithyasoundhar.s@intel.com,\n\nI am working on State Sensor Infra that will creates multiple D-Bus object within a single terminus (ideally it will create D-Bus object for each mention entity within the PDR).\n\nDesign docs:\nhttps://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/docs/+/92069\n\nPLDM Implementation:\nhttps://gerrit.openbmc.org/q/topic:%22pldm_state_sensor_support%22\n\nUnder such circumstances, adding Entity Instance Number as suffix doesn\u0027t resolves the naming problem. Instead, I have proposed to use suffix with the following format:\n```\n/\u003cTerminusName\u003e_Container_\u003cContainerID\u003e_\u003cEntityType\u003e_\u003cEntityInstanceNumber\u003e\n```\nwhere `\u003cTerminusName\u003e` will be `Terminus_\u003cTID\u003e` if no aux name has given. \n\nCould we align on that rule there instead of appending the instance number to every terminus name?",
